      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-345067",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n$5xy^{\u2033} + 2y^{\u2032} + 7y = 0$\nLet $y = x^{\u03bb}\u2211_(n = 0)^(\u221e)a_{n}x^{n}$ be a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x = 0$ of the differential equation above.\nGiven that $\u03bb \u2208 (\\frac{1}{2}, 1)$, find the recurrence relation for the coefficients $a_{n}$, where $n = 1, 2, 3, \u2026$.\n\n*Hint: Substituting the Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain\n$5xy^{\u2033}|= 5(\u03bb^{2} - \u03bb)a_{0}x^{\u03bb - 1} + \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)5((\u03bb + n)^{2} - (\u03bb + n))a_{n}x^{\u03bb + n - 1},; 2y^{\u2032}|= 2\u03bba_{0}x^{\u03bb - 1} + \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)2(\u03bb + n)a_{n}x^{\u03bb + n - 1}; 7y|= \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)7a_{n - 1}x^{\u03bb + n - 1}$.*"
