      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-345166",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\nx{y}^{\u2033}+4{y}^{\u2032}+3y=0\n$$\n\nLet $y={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above.\nGiven that $\\lambda \\in (-4,-2),$ find the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,\u2026.$\n\n*Hint: Substituting the Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{\u2033} & =({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ 4{y}^{\u2032} & =4\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\ 3y & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*"
